      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-164150\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">3.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/1945#12461\">Identifying the Local Extrema of a Multivariable Function</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"164150\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionGraphicFrame\"><img class=\"questionGraphic\" src=\"/graphics/q-164150\"/></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>The graph of the function <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"14\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D467 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D453 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is shown above. Which of the points shown are local minimum points?</p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Tue, Oct 13th @ 6:07 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:17</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
